                                                <summary xml:lang="en">Arabic manuscript containing the Old Testament, followed by a fragment of Joseph ben Gorion&apos;s Kitāb aḫbār al-ʿibrāniyyīn.</summary>
                                                <msItem xml:id="ms_Paris_BnF_Arabe_1_item_1">
                                                    <locus from="1v" to="438"/>
                                                    <title xml:lang="fr">Ancien Testament</title>
                                                    <title xml:lang="en">Old Testament</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                    <incipit>
                                                        <quote xml:lang="ar">الحمد لله الواحد الذات المبدع الارض و السموات</quote>
                                                    </incipit>
                                                    <note xml:lang="en">Legacy incipit type: introduction.

[content] The Pentateuch version is attributed in the notice to Saʿīd ibn Yūsuf al-Fayyūmī (Saadia Gaon). A note at f. 296v states that the translation of the Prophets was made from Greek by the priest al-ʿAlam of Alexandria. Another note at f. 404 states that the translation of Proverbs was made by the priest Faḍl Allāh ibn Tādrus in Cairo.

[use] The manuscript served for the Arabic version printed in the Paris Polyglot.</note>
                                                </msItem>
